From 5c00d2d8f5012f2cd1aa7d4cd85762249af9a41a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:10:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 37/38] libretro: time every GPU submission and log stream
 buffer wraps

Each core submission is wrapped in two timestamp writes. The wait thread
logs submissions that ran long on the GPU, started long after the previous
one, or were seen done long after submit, so a periodic stall can be told
apart as GPU work, GPU starvation or late submission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
